<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35171" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδημ-έω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδᾱμέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>live at</i> or <i>in</i> a place, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				9.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).534.6
			</span></i> (Ceos, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>); simply, <i>stay, remain
			in</i> a place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέχρις ἂν ἐνδημῶσιν οἱ πρέσβεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aen.Tact.
					10.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδημῶν καὶ ἀποδημῶν</span>
			Mitteis <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chr.</u>
				284.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, etc.: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ θεὸς ἐνδεδήμηκεν εἰς τὴν ἐμὴν
					ψυχήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					6.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἐν τῷ σώματι, πρὸς τὸν
				Κύριον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Cor.</u>
				5.6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>.</div>
